**Key facts confirmed:**
- r4's router-ID = **14.1.4.1**; it has `area 1 virtual-link 18.1.4.1` pointing to r8
- r8's router-ID = **18.1.4.1**; its OSPF config has **zero** `area 1 virtual-link` statement
- r4's `show ip ospf` reports **"Number of full virtual adjacencies going through this area: 0"** — the virtual link never came up
- r8's OSPF interfaces confirm it is the true ABR: eth0/58.x in area 1, eth1/80.x and all loopbacks in area 2
